Z||000000||atarian||10-03-2001||02:28 AM||||Well first the question... How do you go about cleaning and testing 2.8 fuel injectors? <BR>Now the update... I am from Houston Texas I have gone to Springfield Illinois to pick up a 86 GT that hasn't ran since the late 80's. So I thought, turns out it hasn't ran since 92'. I had the ? about the if the fuel was bad. Well it was; but that was not the big problem. The fuel lines and tank were rusted and the gas tank was emptied from the rust holes. So I went to the Fiero Parts Depot in Paxton Ill. to pick up the parts needed. The old fuel has turned into varnish and coated most of the fuel parts. the rubber parts appear okay but the water pump leaks coolant from the gasket. As far as the old oil it did not turn to sludge but I did put new oil in it anyway. Fan motor was not frozen but did take awhile to spin normal. The engine crank turns freely but starter motor is slow from it sitting so long. Well thats about it, I'll let all of you know if I make it back to Tx A big Thanks to all. God Bless America ! ! ! <p>[This message has been edited by atarian (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||atarian||10-06-2001||05:08 AM||||No response as of yet... need a good shop in pringfield Illinois to take my injectors to thanks again bye...  ||||reg||1
